<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venezuelan War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1810–1823</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence">Spanish American wars of independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Venezuelan War of Independence was the struggle of 1810–1823 in which Venezuelan patriots, led above all by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>, fought Spanish royalist forces. Independence was declared in 1811, but two republics collapsed before Bolívar's victory at Carabobo in 1821 secured the country; the last royalist strongholds fell in 1823, and Venezuela formed part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia until 1830.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venezuelan-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Venezuelan War of Independence" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BatallaCarabobo01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
